<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/071Z">Remark <span data-tag="071Z">9.7.7.5</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="071W" href="/tag/071W">9.7.7.2</a>, suppose that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete. Then, for each $K \in \mathbb {K}$, the full subcategory $\operatorname{Fun}^{ \mathbb {K}-\mathrm{Mult} }( \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \subseteq \operatorname{Fun}( \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ is closed under (levelwise) $K$-indexed colimits; in particular, $\operatorname{Fun}^{ \mathbb {K}-\mathrm{Mult} }( \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ is also $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete (Remark <a data-tag="06BF" href="/tag/06BF">7.6.6.23</a>). Moreover, for every subset $J \subseteq I$, the canonical isomorphism $\operatorname{Fun}( \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \simeq \operatorname{Fun}(\prod _{j \in J} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ j, \operatorname{Fun}( \prod _{ k \in I \setminus J} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ k, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ restricts to an isomorphism of full subcategories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{Fun}^{\mathbb {K}-\mathrm{Mult}}( \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \simeq \operatorname{Fun}^{\mathbb {K}-\mathrm{Mult}}( \prod _{j \in J} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ j, \operatorname{Fun}^{\mathbb {K}-\mathrm{Mult}}( \prod _{ k \in I \setminus J} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ k, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})). \]
</div>
<p> Compare with Remark <a data-tag="070A" href="/tag/070A">9.7.3.3</a>. </p>
</article>
